+
+## JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386)
+
+```ts
+import { applyMergePatch } from "json-toolkit";
+
+applyMergePatch({ a: "b", c: { d: "e" } }, { a: "z", c: { d: null } }); // { a: "z", c: {} }
+```
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)` applies a merge patch and returns the merged document as a new value;
+neither `target` nor `patch` is modified or shared with the result. An object patch is merged member by
+member: a `null` member removes that member of the target, any other member is merged recursively (a
+non-object target is treated as `{}`). Any non-object patch, arrays included, replaces the target as a
+whole; `null` is a valid patch and yields `null`. Because `null` means "remove", a merge patch cannot set a
+member to `null`. `__proto__` and similar keys are ordinary members.
